# width: 120
# height: 40
# The launcher dock on the LEFT edge, auto-hiding, beside the activity
# bar. Two three-cell strips on one edge, and an edge band belongs to
# ONE surface: the dock's three columns are its own whether the strip is
# up or down, and the activity bar starts where they end.
#
# Before the side-band rule the dock's band was one column in name and
# none in fact. The rail painted from column 0 and the dock's grip
# registered a hit down column 0 of three ROWS — two of them the TODOS
# and FINDINGS icons — and, registered last, won them: clicking the left
# edge of the TODOS icon pinned the dock instead of opening the panel
# (hunt/findings-2026-09-21/mouse-side-edge-grip-eats-activity-bar.md).
write a.txt "alpha\n"
open a.txt
ex dock always
ex dock left
ex dock auto
expect screen lacks "dock pinned"
# The dock's own band, off its grip's cells: reserved, painted with the
# frame's ground, answering nothing. The dwell still reveals the strip
# — the band IS the zone — but a press there is not a second way in.
click 0 18
wait 300
expect screen lacks "dock pinned"
# The activity bar's FIRST column on the TODOS row. It is column 3 now,
# outside the dock's band, and all three of the rail's columns are the
# rail's.
click 3 18
wait 300
expect screen contains "TODOS"
